  "notes": [
    "The current offline catalogue has 290 records: 66 sources, 16 products, five offers, three FX observations and 200 benchmarks. Six new Iraqi official source records add ready-mix capability, industrial payroll statistics, a factory rehabilitation directory, a cement price-image lead, a 2025 import-report lead and a notice that indicative construction pricing is being prepared. These records add discovery context, not supplier offers or prices.",
    "The new ready-mix listing reports C15/C25/C30/C36 production and 60–120 m3/h capacity for Baghdad facilities, but does not establish project allocation, mix design, concrete test results, delivery, pumping price or suitability for prestressed guideway beams.",
    "Official 2024 industrial statistics report annual average payroll of IQD 12.5 million at large and IQD 6.3 million at medium establishments. These are annual factory-worker wage statistics, not hourly skilled railway-fabrication charge-out rates, and have not been converted into cost estimates.",
    "The official 2025 import report has not been downloaded, table-extracted or unit-normalized; no material quantity or unit-price observation was added from it. Iraqi Cement State Company price tiles are image-only and remain unparsed. The Ministry indicative construction-price bulletin is described as under preparation and contributes no rates.",
    "The six generic domestic-fabrication screens use exact available material observations, declared labour hours, and an explicit 20% uplift applied to direct known material plus direct base wage. The uplift is unallocated; labour cycles are planning assumptions, not timed factory routes; employer charges, utilities, tooling, QA, waste, tax, transport and installation remain excluded unless explicitly represented.",
    "Source-bound packets v5, candidate material takeoff v4, regional cost reference v4, procurement package BOM v4 and GFRP local-fabrication screen v5 were regenerated from the current source set. Semantic replay passed for the vehicle, federation and three laminate studies. These digital sourcing records do not establish physical qualification or supplier acceptance."
  ],
